Objective Statement

Formal Objective

The Adaptive Vehicle Intelligence Architecture (AVIA) shall interpret relevant observations of the operating environment to establish and maintain an operational context that represents the relationships, significance, and changes necessary to support adaptive decision-making.

---

Objective Intent

Establish the system's capability to transform relevant observations into an interpreted representation of the current operating context while maintaining appropriate separation between interpretation and subsequent decision generation.

---

Success Criteria

This objective is considered satisfied when the system demonstrates the ability to:

- Establish meaningful relationships among relevant observations.
- Determine the operational significance of observed conditions.
- Maintain an up-to-date representation of the operating context.
- Identify relevant changes in operating context.
- Represent interpretation confidence and uncertainty where appropriate.
- Provide an interpreted context suitable for downstream adaptive decision-making.

---

Engineering Constraints

- The objective shall remain solution-independent.
- The objective shall not prescribe specific reasoning algorithms, models, hardware, or software implementations.
- Interpretation shall remain distinct from raw observation and action selection.
- The objective shall not prescribe which action the vehicle should take.
- All derived interpretation objectives shall remain traceable to SO-F-003.

---

Assumptions

- SO-F-002 provides relevant observations of the operating environment.
- Observations may be incomplete, uncertain, or subject to change.
- Subsequent objectives will use the interpreted operating context for adaptive decision generation.
- Decision authority and action execution remain outside the responsibility of this objective.
